{"parentUuid":"3b37b188-db40-4f3c-9791-58250d42ef30","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0179Jrjf3HMx3H131m1Buoph","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MiniZinc Challenge 2025 results main track winners\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2025 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/\"},{\"title\":\"Home | MiniZinc Challenge 2025\",\"url\":\"https://challenge.minizinc.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Modeling Challenge |\",\"url\":\"https://dmcommunity.org/2025/08/19/constraint-modeling-challenge/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - MiniZinc/mzn-challenge: An archive repository containing the MiniZinc instances used for the MiniZinc Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MiniZinc/mzn-challenge\"},{\"title\":\"The SAT Competition - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/competitions.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hakan Kjellerstrand - MiniZinc Challenge 2025 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hakank_minizinc-challenge-2025-results-activity-7366861519315156992-vli1\"},{\"title\":\"On Benchmarking MiniZinc and the LinkedIn Queens Problem - zayenz.se\",\"url\":\"https://zayenz.se/blog/post/benchmarking-linkedin-queens/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the MiniZinc Challenge 2025 results. Google OR-Tools won all the medals in the 2025 challenge. However, the search results don't provide the specific medal winners broken down by category for the main track (such as gold, silver, and bronze medals for each search category).\n\nTo get more detailed information about the specific main track winners and medal placements, you would need to visit the official MiniZinc Challenge 2025 results page at https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/, which appears to contain the complete competition results with detailed scoring tables organized by solver and benchmark category.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d53e0fd3-ada0-4ae7-a350-d34086a9a845","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:36.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b37b188-db40-4f3c-9791-58250d42ef30","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8f414194-3f77-406f-a17c-994a8404e6ca","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPepzvcBu36X17o5M67WCP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MiniZinc Challenge 2024 results winners CP-SAT Chuffed Gecode\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/\"},{\"title\":\"Differential cryptanalysis with SAT, SMT, MILP, and CP\",\"url\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/105.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"3.5. Solving Technologies and Solver Backends — The MiniZinc Handbook 2.9.7\",\"url\":\"https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/stable/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2023 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2023/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2025 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - chuffed/chuffed: The Chuffed CP solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2016 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2016/results/\"},{\"title\":\"3.1. The MiniZinc Command Line Tool — The MiniZinc Handbook 2.9.5\",\"url\":\"https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/2.9.5/command_line.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the MiniZinc Challenge 2024. The first result is from the official MiniZinc Challenge 2024 results page, which lists the participating solvers including CP-SAT, Chuffed, and Gecode. However, the specific search result snippet doesn't show the actual winners or final rankings - it only lists the participating solvers and their descriptions.\n\nOR-Tools CP-SAT, Chuffed, and Gecode were among the solvers that participated in the MiniZinc Challenge 2024. The search result shows these were listed on the official results page, but the specific snippet doesn't contain the actual winners or medal rankings.\n\nTo get the detailed results and winners for the 2024 challenge, you would need to visit the full results page at https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/ directly, as the search results only show the list of participating solvers rather than the final rankings and winners.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d3291806-9769-439e-b0b5-961bcb5c9b8d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:36.954Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f414194-3f77-406f-a17c-994a8404e6ca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"baf4e0f2-f7ea-4248-b51f-67a192193199","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HJUAskiyvVAHS21bdfvLr1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Choco solver 4.10 user propagator incremental API rectangle packing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.10.1 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.10.1/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.0.2 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.0.2/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.0.3 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.0.3/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Release 4.10.7 · chocoteam/choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chocoteam/choco-solver/releases/tag/4.10.7\"},{\"title\":\"PropLoadToItem (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.0.9 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.0.9/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/nary/binPacking/PropLoadToItem.html\"},{\"title\":\"Designing a propagator | Choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://choco-solver.org/docs/advanced-usages/propagator/\"},{\"title\":\"choco-solver/CHANGES.md at master · chocoteam/choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chocoteam/choco-solver/blob/master/CHANGES.md\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 3.3.0 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/3.3.0/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Uses of Class org.chocosolver.solver.constraints.Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.0.2 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.0.2/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/class-use/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 3.3.1 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/3.3.1/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Choco solver 4.10 and its propagator API with incremental filtering support. Here's what I found:\n\n## Choco Solver 4.10 Propagator and Incremental API\n\nThe incremental filtering algorithm is defined within the Propagator and is called whenever the variable has changed. The boolean argument in the propagator constructor allows you to specify if the propagator is incremental, and when set to true, the method propagate(int varIdx, int mask) must be implemented.\n\n### Key Components:\n\nA new propagator is created to filter the domains of variables with a priority and a boolean parameter indicating whether the propagator must be informed of every variable modification.\n\nThe method propagate(int varIdx, int mask) defines the incremental filtering and is called for every variable whose domain has changed since the last call.\n\nThe method getPropagationConditions(int vIdx) enables not to react on every kind of domain modification.\n\n### Regarding Rectangle Packing:\n\nThe search results did not contain specific information about rectangle packing implementations in Choco solver 4.10. However, the results do show that there are incremental propagators for bin packing constraints that propagate bin loads to item/bin allocations. Rectangle packing would likely use similar incremental propagator patterns, though the specific implementation details were not found in these results.\n\nIf you need more specific information about rectangle packing in Choco 4.10, I can search for additional resources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b46e3137-edc3-447f-8307-726abb111ae8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:41.136Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"baf4e0f2-f7ea-4248-b51f-67a192193199","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"185ad510-4f73-448b-b800-3762de600ebf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W8KTqJ5jeX94wFWhrYTNty","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Chuffed solver lazy clause generation learned clause export incremental\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Chuffed, a lazy clause generation solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"FreshPorts -- math/chuffed: Lazy clause generation CP solver for MiniZinc\",\"url\":\"https://www.freshports.org/math/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"chuffed/DESCRIPTION at master · chuffed/chuffed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed/blob/master/DESCRIPTION\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetries and Lazy Clause Generation ∗ Geoffrey Chu and Peter J. Stuckey\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/11/Papers/094.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bug#1063388: ITP: chuffed -- lazy clause generation CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://lists.debian.org/debian-devel/2024/02/msg00078.html\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation Reengineered | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221633085_Lazy_Clause_Generation_Reengineered\"},{\"title\":\"Bug#1063388: ITP: chuffed -- lazy clause generation CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.mail-archive.com/debian-science@lists.debian.org/msg13858.html\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Variable Activity Initialisation for Lazy Clause Generation Solvers | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-78230-6_4\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Symmetries and Lazy Clause Generation.\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220814076_Symmetries_and_Lazy_Clause_Generation\"},{\"title\":\"Implicit Conflict-Based Search Using Lazy Clause Generation\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/ICAPS/article/download/3471/3339/6520\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Chuffed and lazy clause generation:\n\n## Chuffed Solver Overview\n\nChuffed is a state of the art lazy clause solver designed from the ground up with lazy clause generation in mind. Lazy clause generation is a hybrid approach to constraint solving that combines features of finite domain propagation and Boolean satisfiability.\n\n## Key Features Related to Your Query\n\n**Lazy Clause Generation:**\nFinite domain propagation is instrumented to record the reasons for each propagation step. This creates an implication graph like that built by a SAT solver, which may be used to create efficient nogoods that record the reasons for failure. These nogoods can be propagated efficiently using SAT unit propagation technology.\n\n**Variable Handling:**\nFor \"small\" variables (|D| <= 1000), SAT variables representing [x = v] or [x >= v] are eagerly created at the start of the problem. For \"large\" variables (|D| > 1000), the SAT variables are lazily generated as needed.\n\n**Learned Clause Export:**\nThe search results contain references to learned clause handling in Chuffed, with research showing how the learning solver Chuffed can be instrumented to produce detailed records of its execution, enabling users to measure the impact of the learnt clauses.\n\n**Incremental Support:**\nThe easiest way to use Chuffed is as a backend to the MiniZinc constraint modelling language. This enables incremental problem-solving through the MiniZinc interface.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cb408b3e-020f-496c-836f-8014b268a4b1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:41.237Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"185ad510-4f73-448b-b800-3762de600ebf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
