{"parentUuid":"4b875992-6234-4ac7-8cac-0c9b5d28b36b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EZq8pc3L7fFmzxGruLozGk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT learned clause export limitation extract nogoods\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and learned clauses:\n\nRestarts rebuild the search tree from scratch, but keep learned clauses, which allows the solver to recover from bad decisions and lead to smaller search trees by learning from the mistakes of the past.\n\nThe search results also reference nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree, which help avoid exploring the same subtrees as one another in the context of shared tree workers in CP-SAT.\n\nAdditionally, clause learning is critical as it offsets the cost of running the simplex in CP-SAT.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about limitations on learned clause export or extracting nogoods. If you're looking for more detailed technical documentation on this specific feature, you may want to check the official OR-Tools GitHub repository or the detailed API documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9b6cb8af-cb08-46bc-b792-64be3a6cc9e1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:03.775Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b875992-6234-4ac7-8cac-0c9b5d28b36b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43489813-743e-44fa-94ab-c624edf23f7a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CqjKk51mcSUPboYKz7vWNi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gecode 6.3 incremental learned clause export user propagator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advisors for Incremental Propagation Mikael Z. Lagerkvist and Christian Schulte\",\"url\":\"http://www.gecode.dev/papers/LagerkvistSchulte_CP_2007.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode: Integer propagators\",\"url\":\"http://www.gecode.dev/doc-latest/reference/group__FuncIntProp.html\"},{\"title\":\"gecode/changelog.in at master · Gecode/gecode\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Gecode/gecode/blob/master/changelog.in\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode: Integer modification events and propagation conditions\",\"url\":\"https://www.gecode.org/doc/6.2.0/reference/group__TaskActorIntMEPC.html\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode - Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://mathforprogramming.github.io/logic/lecture05.html\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode: Graph constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.gecode.dev/doc-latest/reference/group__TaskModelIntGraph.html\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode: Gecode::PropagatorGroup Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://www.gecode.org/doc/6.2.0/reference/classGecode_1_1PropagatorGroup.html\"},{\"title\":\"[gecode-users] Watching Propagators\",\"url\":\"https://www.gecode.org/users-archive/2011-June/003305.html\"},{\"title\":\"My Constraint Programming Blog: Gecode Archives\",\"url\":\"https://www.hakank.org/constraint_programming_blog/gecode/\"},{\"title\":\"Gecode: Changelog\",\"url\":\"https://www.gecode.org/doc-latest/reference/PageChange.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about Gecode and its features, though the results don't contain specific details about all the combined terms in your query.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**Incremental Propagation in Gecode:**\n\nGecode added a CachedView that can cache the domain between propagator invocations and provides an efficient test whether a view has changed since the previous invocation as well as an iterator over the removed domain values, making it easier to implement incremental propagation algorithms that need exact delta information.\n\n**User Propagators:**\n\nGecode allows users to extend it by programming their own propagators, with several possible propagators to choose from.\n\n**Propagation and Variables:**\n\nDuring propagation, the domain and the tell provide information to an advisor which variable has changed and how it has changed.\n\nThe search results contain general information about Gecode's constraint propagation system, advisors for incremental propagation, and user-defined propagators, but they don't specifically address the combination of \"learned clause export\" and version 6.3 features that you're asking about. For more detailed information about these specific features in Gecode 6.3, you may want to consult the official Gecode documentation or release notes for that specific version.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"90d23489-47ff-438a-ba34-e284d7a826f0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:03.931Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43489813-743e-44fa-94ab-c624edf23f7a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4499a61a-e4ab-4a3c-a142-9d96852bf90a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YEwKsPwLBaygGZhkgQQY9C","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Picat SAT solver 3.6 CSP compilation MiniZinc challenge 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PicatSAT: A SAT Compiler in Picat\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_picatsat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-use-global-constraints_tbl3_305780906\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Picat-SAT Compiler\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305780906_The_Picat-SAT_Compiler\"},{\"title\":\"The Picat-SAT Compiler Neng-Fa Zhou1 and H˚akan Kjellerstrand2\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/padl16.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc with Picat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/mBmQL6gXKP0\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/cp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PicatSat - getting started\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/picat-lang/c/brPp8u82x3w\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that do not use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-do-not-use-global-constraints_tbl2_305780906\"},{\"title\":\"The Picat-SAT Compiler | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-28228-2_4\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Picat SAT solver 3.6 and its role in CSP compilation for the MiniZinc Challenge 2024:\n\n## PicatSAT Overview\n\nPicat provides facilities for solving combinatorial search problems, including a common interface with CP, SAT, and MIP solvers, tabling for dynamic programming, and a module for planning. PicatSAT was one of the solvers that competed in the MiniZinc Challenge 2024.\n\n## SAT Compilation Technology\n\nPicatSAT is a pure eager SAT compiler based on the log encoding, and PicatSAT won the main tracks in the XCSP3 Competition 2019 and 2022, and has ranked highly in every MiniZinc Challenge since 2016.\n\n## Key Technical Features\n\nPicatSAT adopts the sign-and-magnitude log encoding for domain variables. For a domain with the maximum absolute value n, it uses log2(n) Boolean variables to encode the domain. If the domain contains both negative and positive values, then another Boolean variable is employed to encode the sign.\n\nPicatSAT adopts some well-known optimizations from CP systems, language compilers, and hardware design systems for encoding constraints into compact and efficient SAT code. PicatSAT is also empowered by a novel optimization, called equivalence reasoning, for arithmetic constraints, which leads to reduction of code size and execution time.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b1bc282b-59f7-4ac8-8725-a9027440752a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:05.220Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4499a61a-e4ab-4a3c-a142-9d96852bf90a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9444a7e6-f1d7-40ef-b64e-f112aa716c4e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xcXHrgmXuqnaPpxvqq5nP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pumpkin solver Rust LCG 2024 2025 lazy clause generation MiniZinc\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"Minizinc\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_pumpkin.txt\"},{\"title\":\"pumpkin_solver - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver/latest/pumpkin_solver/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\"},{\"title\":\"Pumpkin/pumpkin-solver/src/propagators/element.rs at main · ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin/blob/main/pumpkin-solver/src/propagators/element.rs\"},{\"title\":\"My Constraint Programming Blog: MiniZinc: the lazy clause generation solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.hakank.org/constraint_programming_blog/2009/08/minizinc_the_lazy_clause_gener.html\"},{\"title\":\"Chuffed, a lazy clause generation solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"On Benchmarking MiniZinc and the LinkedIn Queens Problem - zayenz.se\",\"url\":\"https://zayenz.se/blog/post/benchmarking-linkedin-queens/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2025 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2016 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2016/results/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Pumpkin:\n\n## Overview\n\nPumpkin is a new combinatorial optimisation solver that is under active development at the ConSol Lab at TU Delft. The solver is written in pure Rust and also exposes a Rust API which allows users to express models with predefined constraints and implement custom branching strategies.\n\n## Core Technology\n\nThe solver is based on the (lazy clause generation) constraint programming paradigm. It supports integer variables, the FlatZinc built-in constraints for integer and boolean variables, and the cumulative global constraint.\n\n## Features and Capabilities\n\nPumpkin has a FlatZinc frontend, but can also be used to solve SAT and MaxSAT problems. A unique feature of Pumpkin is that it can produce a certificate of unsatisfiability as part of the solving process without significant overhead.\n\n## MiniZinc Integration\n\nUsers can add the path to pumpkin to the MZN_SOLVER_PATH environment variable to integrate it with MiniZinc. Pumpkin participated in the MiniZinc Challenge 2024, and continues to be actively developed with recent updates noted in 2025.\n\n## Development Team\n\nThe contributors of Pumpkin are (in alphabetical order): Emir Demirović, Maarten Flippo, Imko Marijnissen, Konstantin Sidorov, and Jeff Smits.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"188e1cf3-c982-4326-83a5-2b1e27258efa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:06.953Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9444a7e6-f1d7-40ef-b64e-f112aa716c4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
