{"parentUuid":"2e08c4b4-9c4f-4438-b361-bc90bb9ecbfe","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJqWi3x897RuBsnea1vmWa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Toulbar2 weighted CSP 2D placement benchmark 1.2 incremental\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Presentation — toulbar2 1.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://toulbar2.github.io/toulbar2/\"},{\"title\":\"ToolBarIntro\",\"url\":\"https://carlit.toulouse.inra.fr/cgi-bin/awki.cgi/ToolBarIntro\"},{\"title\":\"C++ Library — toulbar2 1.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://toulbar2.github.io/toulbar2/ref/ref_cpp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Publications — toulbar2 1.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://toulbar2.github.io/toulbar2/publications.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - toulbar2/toulbar2: Exact optimization for cost function networks and additive graphical models\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toulbar2/toulbar2\"},{\"title\":\"Numberjack/Numberjack/solvers/Toulbar2 at master · eomahony/Numberjack\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/eomahony/Numberjack/tree/master/Numberjack/solvers/Toulbar2\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Max-CSP competition 2008: toulbar2 solver description\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/242297950_Max-CSP_competition_2008_toulbar2_solver_description\"},{\"title\":\"toulbar2/CMakeLists.txt at master · toulbar2/toulbar2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toulbar2/toulbar2/blob/master/CMakeLists.txt\"},{\"title\":\"Max-CSP competition 2008: toulbar2 solver description | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/242093522_Max-CSP_competition_2008_toulbar2_solver_description\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · toulbar2/toulbar2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toulbar2/toulbar2/releases\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about Toulbar2 and some of its features. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Toulbar2: Weighted CSP Solver\n\nToulbar2 is an open-source black-box C++ optimizer for cost function networks and discrete additive graphical models. This also covers Max-SAT, Max-Cut, QUBO (and constrained variants), among others.\n\n### Key Capabilities\n\nToulbar2 won several medals in competitions on Max-CSP/COP (CPAI08, XCSP3 2022, 2023, and 2024) and probabilistic graphical models (UAI 2008, 2010, 2014, 2022 MAP task).\n\n### Incremental Solving\n\nRegarding incremental solving, Toulbar2 1.1.0 includes a Python3 API (based on pybind), the ability to do incremental solving, to produce sequences of solutions with guaranteed diversity, pseudo-boolean constraints, a new reader for pseudo-boolean problems (.opb format) and new VAC-based variable ordering and upper-bounding heuristics.\n\nThe search results provide general information about Toulbar2's capabilities with weighted CSP solving and incremental solving features, though specific details about a \"2D placement benchmark 1.2\" were not found in these results. If you're looking for more specific benchmark information or documentation, you may want to check the official Toulbar2 GitHub repository or documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8b9460e2-1047-4224-b977-0aa3dbd662de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:17.027Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e08c4b4-9c4f-4438-b361-bc90bb9ecbfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b5fd3a7b-e926-4b76-8188-d6e0ad08e89f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VhnKkdhpPcs46U9oa5X4Ln","type":"tool_result","content":"# Chuffed vs OR-Tools CP-SAT\n\nBased on the GitHub repository content provided, I can identify several capabilities mentioned for Chuffed:\n\n**Documented Features:**\n- \"Assumption interface\" with FlatZinc hooks for internal assumption handling\n- Integration with CP Profiler for search tree visualization\n- MiniZinc backend support (fzn-chuffed executable)\n- C++ API for direct usage\n- Lazy clause generation technology producing \"nogood\" clauses\n- VSIDS variable selection heuristic\n- Global propagators (alldiff, inverse, minimum, table, regular, mdd, cumulative, disjunctive, circuit, difference)\n\n**Notable Capabilities:**\nThe documentation emphasizes that Chuffed \"combines features of finite domain propagation and Boolean satisfiability,\" with instrumented propagation that records reasoning for each step.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nThe provided content does not include information about Python bindings, and no version numbers are visible in this GitHub page excerpt. The documentation does not compare Chuffed directly to OR-Tools CP-SAT, so I cannot definitively state what unique advantages Chuffed offers relative to that solver based solely on this source material.\n\nTo make an accurate comparison, you would need to consult Chuffed's documentation or academic papers describing its specific architectural differences from OR-Tools."}]},"uuid":"78862c13-7288-4b23-b4ee-75b4a7576801","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:18.446Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5fd3a7b-e926-4b76-8188-d6e0ad08e89f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5c0d895e-dd8a-4aaf-95f4-4de159649cfc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NtuRmjZgkcFi7g2BX7zVLa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP Optimizer\" 2D rectangle packing strip packing benchmark vs CP-SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking: 2D Strip Packing problem solved with different approaches\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking/README.md at master · johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - eskinderit/2D-Strip-Packing-Problem: Solving the 2D Strip Packing problem with mutiple optimization techniques.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/eskinderit/2D-Strip-Packing-Problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A SAT-based Method for Solving the Two-dimensional Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220445013_A_SAT-based_Method_for_Solving_the_Two-dimensional_Strip_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal rectangle packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220462008_Optimal_rectangle_packing\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal rectangle packing | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-008-0463-6\"},{\"title\":\"Survey for 2-D packing algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://cgi.csc.liv.ac.uk/~epa/surveyhtml.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about approaches to solving 2D rectangle packing and strip packing problems using constraint programming and CP-SAT. Here's what the search reveals:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nOne implementation uses google's CP-SAT to solve 2D knapsack problems with a time limit of 1 second, demonstrating CP-SAT's application to packing subproblems.\n\nThere are implementations of the 2D Strip Packing problem using different approaches of combinatorial optimization, including constraint programming implementations and SAT solver approaches in both constrained SAT formulation and the more expressive SMT one.\n\nCP-SAT features interval variables that become interesting in combination with no-overlap constraints for 1D and 2D, which can be used for geometric packing problems and scheduling problems where overlaps must be prevented. The add_no_overlap_2d constraint is used to ensure that no two rectangles overlap.\n\nRegarding benchmarking, a branch-and-cut algorithm produces optimal solutions for the majority of 500 benchmark instances in less than 20 minutes, though it has difficulty in proving feasibility/infeasibility of 2D orthogonal packing subproblems for instances with many small items.\n\nThe search results show that both CP Optimizer (via or-tools) and CP-SAT are used for 2D packing problems, but the results don't contain direct performance comparisons between CP Optimizer and CP-SAT on standard benchmarks. For a detailed benchmark comparison between these specific solvers, you may need to consult more specialized literature or solver-specific documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"46c415ba-bde2-448e-8f97-bf4f2e99d89b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:19.220Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c0d895e-dd8a-4aaf-95f4-4de159649cfc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0b8ebccb-a789-41cb-9a6b-41c11b34a009","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRs8ZwEsVGQzQuRDFNfeEA","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pumpkin Solver Features\n\nBased on the GitHub repository, here's what Pumpkin offers:\n\n**Confirmed Features:**\n- **Lazy Clause Generation**: Core constraint programming paradigm\n- **Certificates of Unsatisfiability**: \"A unique feature of Pumpkin is that it can produce a certificate of unsatisfiability\"\n- **MiniZinc Support**: Functions as a backend solver for MiniZinc modeling language\n- **Language Bindings**: Python bindings available via pumpkin-solver-py\n- **Global Constraints**: Cumulative, disjunctive, element, arithmetic constraints, and clausal constraints\n\n**Not Mentioned:**\nThe documentation does not discuss learned clause export, incremental solving, user propagator API, or performance comparisons with Chuffed or CP-SAT.\n\n**Version:**\nCurrent version is **0.3.0** (released February 11, 2026)\n\n**Installation:**\nAvailable as Rust library (`cargo add pumpkin-solver`), CLI tool (`cargo install pumpkin-solver`), and Python package on PyPI.\n\n**Recognition:**\nWon bronze medal in the 2025 MiniZinc Challenge's fixed search track."}]},"uuid":"d44a30de-c7ea-49a8-9e7f-543ee5599b63","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:19.544Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b8ebccb-a789-41cb-9a6b-41c11b34a009","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
