{"parentUuid":"7947d8ae-8181-46c7-b063-544aa8ed0e0a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012qGgSJnn1gVZTMb98EKB11","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP Optimizer interval variables placement IBM benchmark vs OR-Tools 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) IBM ILOG CP optimizer for scheduling: 20+ years of scheduling with constraints at IBM/ILOG\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/323859275_IBM_ILOG_CP_optimizer_for_scheduling_20_years_of_scheduling_with_constraints_at_IBMILOG\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CP Optimizer for Detailed Scheduling Illustrated on Three Problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353689_IBM_ILOG_CP_Optimizer_for_Detailed_Scheduling_Illustrated_on_Three_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - IBMDecisionOptimization/cpofzn: CP Optimizer back end for Minizinc · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/IBMDecisionOptimization/cpofzn\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, CP Optimizer, OR-Tools, Gurobi, Cplex on very large-scale instances of the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CP Optimizer for Detailed Scheduling Illustrated on Three Problems\",\"url\":\"https://cse.unl.edu/~choueiry/F14-421-821/Documents/Laborie-CPAIOR-2009.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CP Optimizer V2.3 Getting Started with IBM ILOG CP Optimizer\",\"url\":\"https://public.dhe.ibm.com/software/websphere/ilog/docs/optimization/cpoptimizer/gscpoptimizer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Temporal linear relaxation in IBM ILOG CP Optimizer | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/286227727_Temporal_linear_relaxation_in_IBM_ILOG_CP_Optimizer\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CP optimizer for scheduling | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-018-9281-x\"},{\"title\":\"IBM ILOG CPLEX Optimization Studio CP Optimizer User’s Manual\",\"url\":\"https://public.dhe.ibm.com/software/products/Decision_Optimization/docs/pdf/usrcpoptimizer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Interval variables in CP Optimizer\",\"url\":\"https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/20.1.0?topic=concepts-interval-variables-in-cp-optimizer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CP Optimizer interval variables and some benchmark comparisons, though specific 2024 benchmark data comparing interval variable placement between CP Optimizer and OR-Tools was not directly available in the results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## CP Optimizer Interval Variables\n\nAbsent interval variables have special meaning, where an absent interval variable is not considered by any constraint in which it is involved. An important additional feature of interval variables is the fact that they can be optional; in other words, one can decide not to consider them in the solution schedule.\n\n## Benchmark Comparisons\n\nA recent comparison study (November 2025) benchmarked multiple solvers including CP Optimizer and OR-Tools. The comparison includes IBM ILOG CP Optimizer 12.10.0 and Google OR-Tools CP-SAT 9.14. On large-scale Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP) instances with 1,000 jobs and 1,000 machines: Hexaly's results after 10 minutes of computation are, on average, 8.5% better than CP Optimizer's after 6 hours. Notably, OR-Tools, Gurobi, and Cplex fail to deliver feasible solutions within 6 hours of running time.\n\nThe research also notes that analyzing different encodings of the JSSP measures the impact of high-level structures (such as interval variables and no-overlap constraints) on the problem solution.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific 2024 benchmarks focused specifically on interval variable placement strategies between CP Optimizer and OR-Tools. You may want to search IBM's official documentation or recent academic papers for more targeted 2024-specific comparisons.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0987587e-bf23-4fe3-9f5c-7a5fc23b27d8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:30.477Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7947d8ae-8181-46c7-b063-544aa8ed0e0a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e2ea6b79-b3b2-4306-8cf3-a604ac2edc47","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbUquN674dpMKe8RJhEQb3","type":"tool_result","content":"# Hexaly Benchmark Categories\n\nBased on the webpage content, Hexaly publishes benchmarks across these main categories:\n\n**Routing & Logistics:**\n- Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem (CVRP)\n- Vehicle Routing with Time Windows (CVRPTW)\n- Pickup and Delivery with Time Windows (PDPTW)\n- Traveling Salesman Problem (TSP)\n\n**Scheduling:**\n- Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\n- Flexible Job Shop Scheduling (FJSP)\n- Resource-Constrained Project Scheduling (RCPSP)\n- Assembly Line Balancing (SALBP)\n\n**Packing & Clustering:**\n- Bin Packing Problem (BPP)\n- Vector Bin Packing (VBP)\n- Bin Packing with Conflicts (BPPC)\n- K-Means Clustering (MSSC)\n\n**Specialized Problems:**\n- Quadratic Assignment Problem (QAP)\n- Aircraft Landing Problem\n- Inventory Routing Problem (IRP)\n- Car Sequencing with Paint-Shop Batching\n\n**Important Note:** The webpage does not provide specific 2D rectangle packing benchmarks or detailed numerical results. It describes benchmarks as using \"1-minute runtime limits\" on standardized hardware, but specific performance numbers are not included in this page content."}]},"uuid":"bca7c6b6-cfbe-4ebf-a3aa-0cc7856b4d6d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:31.730Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2ea6b79-b3b2-4306-8cf3-a604ac2edc47","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bca7c6b6-cfbe-4ebf-a3aa-0cc7856b4d6d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6d508ceece21642a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q6n1rPiCAbVr6N2L1Vz6HZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"已有充足信息整理报告。\n\n---\n\n# OR-Tools 之外主流 CP/CSP 求解器调研\n\n## 1. 横向对比表（截至 2026-05）\n\n| Solver | 版本 | LCG | Incremental | Learned Clause Export | User Propagator | 内置对称破缺 | License | MZN'24/'25 表现 | 适合我们 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **OR-Tools CP-SAT** | 9.15.6755 | 部分（CDCL） | 弱（仅 AddHint） | **不支持** | 无（只有 callback） | 部分 | Apache 2.0 | 4 项金牌 / 4 项金牌 | 当前主求解器 |\n| **Chuffed** | 0.13.x | **是（原生 LCG）** | MiniZinc 层 + assumption 接口 | C++ 层可拿到 nogood，无官方 Python API | C++ 层可写 | 是（参考 Chu/Stuckey 2011） | MIT | 组织方测试，不参赛 | **强候选**：Benders 子问题 |\n| **Choco-solver** | 4.10.17 | 否 | 是（Java native） | 否 | **是（成熟 Java API）** | 是 | BSD 4-clause | Fixed 银 / Fixed 银+Free 铜+Parallel 铜 | 中等 |\n| **Gecode** | 6.3.0 | 否 | **是（CachedView + Advisor）** | 否 | **是（C++ 一等公民）** | 是（LDSB） | MIT | 多年未参赛 | 可做学术对照，工业上落后 |\n| **JaCoP** | 4.10 | 否 | 弱 | 否 | 是（Java） | 部分 | AGPL | 未参赛 | 不建议（AGPL 传染） |\n| **Picat / PicatSAT** | 3.9 / 3.6 | SAT 编译路线 | 否（编译式） | 通过底层 SAT solver | 否 | 是（编码层） | Mozilla PL | Free 银 / Parallel 银（'24 '25 都是） | 探索式编码实验 |\n| **Pumpkin** | **0.3.0**（2026-02 新出） | **是（Rust 原生 LCG）** | 是（Rust API） | **是 + UNSAT 证书** | 是（Rust trait） | 部分 | MIT | Fixed 铜（2025） | **新兴黑马**：研究/取证场景 |\n| **CP Optimizer** | 22.1.1 | 否（自有 SAT-like 学习） | 是（C++ / Python docplex） | 否 | 否（黑盒） | 是 | 商业（学术免费 CPLEX Studio） | 不参赛 | **scheduling/interval 强**，placement 一般 |\n| **SICStus Prolog** | 4.9 | 否 | 是 | 否 | 是 | 是 | 商业 | Fixed 铜 / Fixed 铜（共享） | 不建议 |\n| **Toulbar2** | 1.2.1 | 否（VAC + bound consistency） | 是（Python pybind） | 否 | 否（黑盒） | 是 | MIT | XCSP3 Max-CSP 多次冠军 | 仅 weighted CSP，不直接适用 |\n| **Hexaly**（前 LocalSolver） | 13.0 | 否（启发式 LS） | 是 | 否 | 否 | N/A | 商业（学术免费） | 不参赛（不是 CP） | 仅做大规模启发对照，**不能给精确证明** |\n| **iZplus** | 内部版本 | 否 | 否 | 否 | 否 | 是 | 学术 | Free 铜 / Parallel 铜 | 不可获取 |\n\n## 2. MiniZinc Challenge 最近成绩简表\n\n**2024**（OR-Tools CP-SAT 4 金 1 LS 金）\n| Track | 金 | 银 | 铜 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fixed | OR-Tools CP-SAT | Choco-solver CP-SAT | SICStus Prolog |\n| Free | OR-Tools CP-SAT | PicatSAT | iZplus |\n| Parallel | OR-Tools CP-SAT | PicatSAT | Choco-solver |\n| Open | OR-Tools CP-SAT | PicatSAT | Choco-solver |\n| Local Search | OR-Tools CP-SAT LS | Yuck | — |\n\n**2025**（OR-Tools 4 金，Open 取消）\n| Track | 金 | 银 | 铜 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fixed | OR-Tools CP-SAT | Choco-solver CP-SAT | SICStus / **Pumpkin** |\n| Free | OR-Tools CP-SAT | PicatSAT | Choco-solver CP-SAT |\n| Parallel | OR-Tools CP-SAT | PicatSAT | iZplus |\n| Local Search | OR-Tools CP-SAT LS | Yuck | Atlantis |\n\n**关键事实**：从 2018 起 OR-Tools CP-SAT 在 MiniZinc Challenge **未输过任何金牌**。Chuffed 和 Gecode 是组织方维护的\"基线\"，不参与评奖。**OR-Tools 在某些 packing/placement 单题被 PicatSAT 反超**（Free 类目分项分中可见），但累计分依然 OR-Tools 第一。\n\n## 3. 针对 placement / 2D packing 的强弱\n\n- **CP-SAT**：`AddNoOverlap2D` + `cp.IntervalVar` 是工业最强组合，2D bin packing 上仍是 SOTA（参考 ktnr/BinPacking2D 的 branch-and-cut 比较）\n- **CP Optimizer**：`intervalVar` + `noOverlap` 模型语义比 CP-SAT 更优雅，但在纯 2D packing 上**没有公开证据击败 CP-SAT**；强项是 **scheduling**（JSSP/RCPSP），不是几何 packing\n- **PicatSAT**：log-encoding SAT 编码，在小 grid 高密度问题表现意外好；但 70x70 的 SAT 编码体量会爆炸\n- **Hexaly**：纯启发式，**不能给精确证明**，仅适合做 baseline 对照——和 Constitution 里\"certified_exact 不能混 exploratory\"冲突，**禁止用作精确路径**\n- **Chuffed (LCG)**：在 Open Shop/Cumulative 类强；2D packing 上历史成绩不如 CP-SAT，但**学到的 nogood 可以喂回主问题**——这是 CP-SAT 做不到的\n\n## 4. 混合使用工程量\n\n- **MiniZinc 一份模型多后端跑**：成本最低。把当前 master/binding/routing 模型导出 FlatZinc 后切 solver 几乎零成本。**实际限制**：CP-SAT 的 `AddHint`、自定义 callback、warm start 这些都不在 FlatZinc 标准里，要丢失。\n- **Python 直接调 Choco/Chuffed**：Choco 有 `pychoco` 绑定（活跃维护），Chuffed 只能走 MiniZinc/FlatZinc 文件转一次，每次启动开销 100ms+\n- **同一项目用多 solver 实战**：**Conflict-Driven CP-LCG 混合** 是公认有效模式（Stuckey 等多篇论文）—— CP-SAT 跑 master，Chuffed/Pumpkin 跑子问题取 nogood，但工程上对接很重\n\n## 5. CP Optimizer (IBM) 单独评估\n\n- **学术 license**：IBM CPLEX Optimization Studio 完全免费学术版（含 CP Optimizer），无需付费\n- **商业 license**：按核数授权，最低档约 **$8000-15000/年**（非公开报价，需联系销售）\n- **强项**：scheduling / `intervalVar` / `cumulative` / `noOverlap` 一维\n- **弱项**：纯几何 placement、**不开源黑盒**、Hexaly 在 JSSP 1000x1000 上 10min 比 CP Optimizer 6 小时还好 8.5%（Hexaly 自家 benchmark，有偏，但 CP Opt 在大规模上确实不强）\n- **对我们项目**：`max_lex(area, min_side)` 不是 scheduling 问题，CP Optimizer **优势用不上**\n\n## 6. 新兴方向\n\n- **Pumpkin** (TU Delft, **0.3.0 / 2026-02 发布**)：Rust 写的 LCG，**能产出 UNSAT 证书**（DRAT-like）。这正好对应 Constitution \"certified_exact\" 路径要求的可审计性。2025 MiniZinc Fixed 拿铜（首次参赛），后续值得跟\n- **Hexaly 13.0** (前 LocalSolver)：纯启发式，对我们精确证明无用\n- **Toulbar2 1.2.1**：weighted CSP / cost function network，问题模型不匹配\n\n## 推荐：如果只能选一个 OR-Tools 之外的 solver\n\n**首选 Chuffed**，用在 **Benders 子问题（routing_subproblem / flow_subproblem）**。\n\n理由：\n1. **LCG 原生支持** — 子问题求 UNSAT 时能给出**最小 nogood 集合**，正好喂给 master_model 的 Benders cut（CP-SAT 完全不支持这条路径）\n2. **MiniZinc 集成成熟**，可以让 binding/routing 各自独立模型化、独立调优\n3. **MIT license**，可商业可再分发，无传染风险\n4. Stuckey 团队 15 年持续维护，工业稳定性 OK\n\n**备选 Pumpkin**：如果想要 **可审计 UNSAT 证书**（对应 Constitution \"exactness\" 要求），且团队接受 Rust 工具链。0.3.0 还很新，1 年内可观察是否成熟。\n\n**不推荐**：CP Optimizer（黑盒 + 无 placement 优势）、Hexaly（纯启发式违反 exactness）、JaCoP（AGPL）、Gecode（工业上已落后）。\n\n---\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- [MiniZinc Challenge 2024 Results](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/)\n- [MiniZinc Challenge 2025 Results](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/)\n- [Chuffed GitHub](https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed)\n- [Pumpkin solver (TU Delft, Rust LCG)](https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin)\n- [Pumpkin docs.rs](https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver/latest/pumpkin_solver/)\n- [Choco-solver Propagator API 4.10](https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.10.1/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html)\n- [Gecode Advisors for Incremental Propagation (Lagerkvist & Schulte, CP 2007)](http://www.gecode.dev/papers/LagerkvistSchulte_CP_2007.pdf)\n- [PicatSAT Compiler (Zhou & Kjellerstrand, PADL 2016)](http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/padl16.pdf)\n- [Toulbar2 GitHub](https://github.com/toulbar2/toulbar2)\n- [IBM CP Optimizer official](https://www.ibm.com/products/ilog-cplex-optimization-studio/cplex-cp-optimizer)\n- [CP Optimizer FlatZinc backend (cpofzn)](https://github.com/IBMDecisionOptimization/cpofzn)\n- [Hexaly Benchmarks](https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks)\n- [Hexaly vs CP Optimizer/OR-Tools/Gurobi on JSSP](https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp)\n- [Symmetries and Lazy Clause Generation, Chu & Stuckey, IJCAI 2011](https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/11/Papers/094.pdf)\n- [BinPacking2D branch-and-cut benchmark](https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2445,"cache_read_input_tokens":38857,"output_tokens":4404,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2445},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4404,"cache_read_input_tokens":38857,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2445,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoqy51Cat9DYh7J2E2gQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9094fa83-68f5-4dc5-8778-a771017d9e3f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:33:48.006Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
